// FUN_000210e8 (cve-2018-21224): the userop VectorSignedToFloat is an ARM NEON
// signed-int -> float conversion (Ghidra ARMneon.sinc). Stock Ghidra declares
// it as a bare `define pcodeop` with no return type, so each call site's
// result is typed undefined<N> by the destination register (undefined4 for the
// S-reg form, undefined8 for the D-reg form) and cast to float/double at the
// use site.
//
// VectorSignedToFloat is registered in the float-returning-userop table, so
// the pipeline resolves the result to a real floating-point type (undefined4
// -> float, undefined8 -> double) and emits a SINGLE declaration whose return
// type is the widest variant (double). The two call sites then cast at the use
// site: double -> float for the undefined4 site (a narrowing convert) and
// double -> double for the undefined8 site (identity). Previously, emitting two
// same-named decls with different undefined4/undefined8 return types collapsed
// them to one CIR symbol and forced a NYI bitcast on the return value (empty
// CIR); the earlier fix split them into return-type-suffixed symbols instead.
//
// CIR-DAG: cir.func{{.*}}@VectorSignedToFloat{{.*}}-> !cir.double
// CIR-NOT: @VectorSignedToFloat_undefined
// CIR-DAG: cir.func dso_local @FUN_000210e8
